{title: Wayfaring Stranger}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Dm}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]I am a poor wayfaring [Gm]stranger,
While [Dm]traveling through this world of [A7]woe;
Yet there's no [Dm]sickness, toil, nor [Gm]danger
In that [F]bright land to which I [A7]go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I'm [F]going there to see my [C]Father,
I'm [F]going there no more to [Bb]roam;
I'm [Dm]only going over [Gm]Jordan,
I'm [Dm]only going over [A7]home. [Dm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [Dm]know dark clouds will [Gm]gather round me,
I [Dm]know my way is rough and [A7]steep;
Yet [Dm]beauteous fields lie [Gm]just before me,
Where [F]God's redeemed their [A7]vigil [Dm]keep.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
